From d31391969563140aec8ffcbc0ecbd55e303fcb45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HBS Hardening Audit <audit@local>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 05:07:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(security): scope MVP analytics requests to the caller's
 company
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- getMvpMetrics() previously aggregated serviceRequests across every
  company on the platform with zero tenant filtering. Any user with
  admin/manager role in ANY company could see combined request counts,
  urgency, and status breakdowns from every other company.
- Now joins serviceRequests -> users on employeeId and filters by
  users.companyId, matching the join pattern already used elsewhere
  in server/db.ts.
- demoRequests and hrSystemPlans remain platform-wide intentionally
  (pre-signup marketing/lead data owned by the HBS team itself, same
  as demoRequestsRouter already treats them) — documented inline.
- Added a regression test asserting the requests query always applies
  a company-scoping WHERE clause.

test(ci): make the test suite reproducible without manual env setup

- 7 tests were failing on a clean checkout because DATABASE_URL and
  HRHBS_ADMIN_EMAIL were not set, even though the underlying code was
  correct (verified by rerunning with the vars set: all 7 passed).
- Added server/_core/vitest.setup.ts with safe, non-networked test
  defaults and wired it into vitest.config.ts.
- Verified no other test relies on DATABASE_URL being absent.

Verified: pnpm check / pnpm test (221/221) / pnpm build all pass clean.
